Description: igOS/Perle: skip UEFI Secure Boot lockdown and shim_lock
 u-boot authenticates this GRUB core against its own UEFI db at bootefi, and the
 core self-enforces kernel/initrd/dtb via the embedded GPG key (--pubkey =>
 check_signatures). There is no shim in the u-boot->GRUB chain, so the shim_lock
 verifier is unavailable, and lockdown disables the `devicetree` command the ARM
 boot needs. Skip both; GPG stays the enforcer. u-boot->GRUB verification is
 unaffected (performed at bootefi, before GRUB executes).
Author: johnlfeeney <johnlfeeney@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-30

--- a/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
@@ -96,10 +96,15 @@
   grub_efi_mm_init ();
 
   /*
-   * Lockdown the GRUB and register the shim_lock verifier
-   * if the UEFI Secure Boot is enabled.
+   * PERLE/igOS: do NOT enter UEFI Secure Boot lockdown or register the
+   * shim_lock verifier. u-boot authenticates this GRUB core against its own
+   * UEFI db before launching it (bootefi), and the core self-enforces
+   * kernel/initrd/dtb via the embedded GPG key (grub-mkstandalone --pubkey =>
+   * check_signatures). There is no shim in the u-boot->GRUB chain (shim_lock
+   * protocol absent), and lockdown would disable the `devicetree` command the
+   * ARM boot requires. GPG remains the enforcer.
    */
-  if (grub_efi_get_secureboot () == GRUB_EFI_SECUREBOOT_MODE_ENABLED)
+  if (0 && grub_efi_get_secureboot () == GRUB_EFI_SECUREBOOT_MODE_ENABLED)
     {
       grub_lockdown ();
       grub_shim_lock_verifier_setup ();
